Yes, when playing slash'em, you should stash certain wands in your bag. 
  A wand of death should be stashed as long as you don't have magic 
resistance.  I once accidentally broke my wand of death in vanilla.  It 
took away a lot of Hp, but I survived, presumably due to my grey dragon 
scale mail.  My pet warhorse took a lot of damage but survived, too - 
for a while.  It was then taken down by a monster.  In slash'em wands 
act similar on exploding as on breaking.

Wands of cancellation should go in a sack or in some chest or box.  You 
should never carry them around in your knapsack.  Well, maybe at the 
beginning of a game, with no enchanted armor, no scrolls and no potions 
nor other wands out of your bag, it may not be too bad.  Of course, you 
should not put a wand of cancellation into your bag of holding.

Other wands that should not be carried are polymorph (can polymorph you 
*and* part of your stuff) and lightning (can cost rings that you more or 
less have to keep outside the bag).  Drain level, unless you are 
wielding Excalibur or Stormbringer or wearing an amulet of protection 
against level draining.  Fire, fire ball, cold are not as bad as soon as 
you have the resistances (just annoying).  Digging is only annoying when 
it explodes.  Create monster and create horde should not be carried 
unless you are strong enough or have a scroll of teleportation 
(preferably blessed) handy.

